# Corpus unit ftrl/C01 — gap (negative-result through the null_comparison dual)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/ftrl.yaml C01 (negative-result, controlled_comparison; corpus pin
# 62e9b54). Headline: vanilla RL fine-tuning fails to leverage pre-trained capabilities and
# ends up comparable to or worse than training from scratch, because of forgetting of pre-
# trained capabilities (FPC) — NetHack vanilla FT collapses to ~1K return (frozen model ~5K);
# RoboticSequence vanilla FT is indistinguishable from scratch with FAR stages at 0% within
# 100K steps; Montezuma Room-7 success drops in the first 20M steps (E01/E02/E03).
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * The claim is genuinely the negation of a comparison conclusion (proposition_shape
#     final_perf_leq(vanilla_ft, from_scratch, ...)), so it lowers through the null_comparison
#     dual: conclusion not_better(vanilla_ft, from_scratch, final_return, rl_envs). The FPC
#     mechanism and per-environment collapse cells live in nl and the leaf refs.
#   * Only one side (not_better) appears, so no contrary/rebut edge is forced (attack
#     completeness is arg-conclusion-level; corpus-v1 §Conflict).
#   * null_comparison's mandatory adequate_power CQ (seeds/uncertainty for every environment)
#     has no discharging leaf: E01 reports 5 seeds and E03 20 seeds/90% CIs, but E02
#     (Montezuma) states no seed count or interval, so the seeds obligation is unmet corpus-
#     wide for this claim. The null_comparison argument is declared as a located hole with
#     `open adequate_power` (lowering re-done for issue #15 under lara-core@0.3; until
#     lara-core@0.2 the open mandatory obligation rejected the unit, so the arg was omitted):
#     it is not an AF node, and the claim lands `gap` on empty complete support.
#     baseline_parity (scratch baseline run per environment) and measurement_validity (FAR-state
#     collapse directly measured) are annotated met and discharged on the hole.
#   * Coverage flag (kind-a, summary §3): the majority quantifier "in most practical scenarios"
#     over an open environment class has no direct construct; it instantiates per tested env in
#     the atom and its class-vs-tested-set scope lives in the binding, audited on faithfulness.
#     E02 expects vanilla FT to finish ABOVE scratch in final return, so the scratch-comparison
#     leg rests on E01/E03 while E02 supports only the FAR-forgetting leg (annotation hole 2).
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact ftrl at sha256:9d5807db04eb
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, not assemblable at corpus-v1's evidential bar --------------------------

claim c01
  nl      = "Vanilla RL fine-tuning fails to leverage pre-trained capabilities: due to forgetting (FPC) its final performance is comparable to or worse than training from scratch across NetHack, Montezuma, and RoboticSequence (NetHack ~1K vs frozen ~5K return; RoboticSequence FAR stages 0% within 100K steps)"
  formal  = not_better(vanilla_ft, from_scratch, final_return, rl_envs)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = reviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: the null comparison against scratch, per result cell across E01/E03 (the
# scratch-comparison legs), folded into refs.
leaf e1 : reports(e01, compares(vanilla_ft, from_scratch, final_return, rl_envs, null))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E01, logic/experiments.md#E03, Figure-3a, Table-4, Table-5, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N06, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N11]

leaf e2 : matched_setup(vanilla_ft, from_scratch, e01)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E01-Procedure-step-4a, logic/experiments.md#E02-Procedure-step-4a, logic/experiments.md#E03-Procedure-step-4a, logic/experiments.md#E01-Baselines]

leaf e3 : valid_measurement(final_return, e01)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E02-step-5, logic/experiments.md#E03-step-5, logic/experiments.md#E01-trajectory-metrics]

# --- ... but only an incomplete argument (a located hole) is declarable -------------------------

# The incomplete argument: adequate_power has no honest leaf — E02/Montezuma reports no seed
# count or uncertainty — and corpus-v1 makes it mandatory, so it stays open and a1 is a hole.
arg a1 : supports(c01) by null_comparison(vanilla_ft, from_scratch, final_return, rl_envs, e01)
  discharge baseline_parity      with e2
  discharge measurement_validity with e3
  open      adequate_power

status c01

# ==============================================================================================
# EXPECTED VERDICT (golden oracle)
# ==============================================================================================
# Compiled AF: no arguments (a1 is a located hole, not an AF node).
# Located hole: a1 (null_comparison), open obligations [adequate_power]; sources no attacks.
# Claim status:
#   c01 -> gap (empty complete support; statusC = Gap iff null claimSupport, spec §8;
#          the hole a1 is reported in the verdict's holes section, not as a node)
